{
  "_readme": "GAME CONTENT, TUNABLE STARTING VALUES PENDING PRODUCER REVIEW (names, stats, sources). Names and descriptions: DRAFT content pass pending producer review; naming rules in docs/design/content-items.md. Every piece of beast gear (Slot a GearSlot name) and avatar gear (Slot an AvatarGearSlot name), in five bands (MinimumLevel 1/21/41/61/81): per band six beast pieces (Striker fang (Attack) / focus stone (SpecialAttack); Bulwark barding (Defense + HP) / warding mantle (SpecialDefense + HP); Swift wind charm (Speed) / keen collar (CritChance)) and three avatar pieces (staff, coat, ring), each as a common (Rarity 0, shop and drops) and a rare (1, shop, drops and lair first clears below band 41; stage passes grant a common of the band); from band 41 an epic (2) of each of the six beast pieces, from lairs only. Budget (GearLibraryValidator, checked by the importer and the EditMode tests against the roster): points = sum(Flat / ref + Pct), ref = the roster mean of the stat at MinimumLevel + 10, Speed x1.5, each CritChance point 0.01; common 5%, rare 8%, epic 12% in the first band, scaled per band by (T(11) / T(MinimumLevel + 10))^0.65 with T the roster mean stat total (about x0.7 / 0.56 / 0.47 / 0.41 for bands 21-81, so a piece worth in levels-equivalent stays about flat, per the balance simulator --economy-probe), +/- 10%, and no piece adds more than 25% to any species stat at its MinimumLevel; MoveRange not allowed. Flat where it rounds cleanly, Pct at the low bands. Generated to budget, then hand-editable. Edit here, then in Unity run Beast Craft/Data/Import Gear Library (after Import Beast Roster). See docs/design/economy-and-shop.md, \"Gear\".",
  "SchemaVersion": 1,
